marie: Qualcomm-only drivers off at compile time (touch, keys, cpufreq, I2C1, USB, modem)

Their TLMM/GCC/SPMI/QUP/DWC3/cpufreq-hw addresses are plain low DRAM on
the Kirin 710. The first eMMC-root boot showed sweet_keys probing SPMI
and sweet_touch scheduling itself (they start with the root device);
boot-args (sweettouch=0 ...) are no longer the only thing in the way.
SweetBattery falls back to its static source (sweet_i2c1_init fails).

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
index 94c7552..3b34798 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
+#include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>   /* SWEET_MARIE */
 #include <machine/machine_routines.h>
 
 extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t, vm_size_t);
@@ -22,7 +23,12 @@ int
 sweet_cpufreq_max(void)
 {
 	int on = 1;
+#if SWEET_MARIE
+	/* marie (Kirin 710): this is Qualcomm hardware; its addresses are plain DRAM there */
+	on = 0;
+#else
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetcpufreq", &on, sizeof(on));
+#endif
 	if (!on) {
 		return 0;
 	}
